1
00:00:00,208 --> 00:00:02,480
(Previously)
I'm friends with a Kongpurim. So what, Dad?

2
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:04,960
You said it was grown-up
business, didn't you?

3
00:00:05,031 --> 00:00:06,751
So it has nothing to do with a kid like me.

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:10,261
I'm stressed because there's
something I want to do,

5
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,606
but I know my family would never approve.

6
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:14,440
Then just do it without letting
them find out. It's that simple.

7
00:00:16,454 --> 00:00:17,800
I think I like you, Blue.

8
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:22,920
And I never want our time together to end.

9
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,761
[Blue: Where are you?]

10
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,801
[Tokyo: I've been waiting
for you, please hurry.]

11
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,680
[Look at what's stuck under the table.]

12
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:02,241
[Share it with someone you like.]

13
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,200
- Tokyo.
- Tokyo.

14
00:02:22,571 --> 00:02:23,572
Oh, hey.

15
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,121
Hey.

16
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,280
- Hey.
- Yeah?

17
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:35,323
Are you okay? Why
are you smiling like that?

18
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:37,701
I'm fine. It's nothing.

19
00:02:38,624 --> 00:02:39,835
Nothing?

20
00:02:40,496 --> 00:02:42,880
I've seen you staring at
your phone for weeks now.

21
00:02:43,382 --> 00:02:45,120
It's nothing.

22
00:02:45,465 --> 00:02:47,680
I was just checking the trending hashtags.

23
00:02:49,907 --> 00:02:52,320
Yeah, whatever. If there's
nothing, then there's nothing.

24
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:59,280
Hey, this evening my band has rehearsal.
We're practicing a new song. Wanna come watch?

25
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,560
- Sure.
- This evening?

26
00:03:01,730 --> 00:03:02,850
I need to go to the library.

27
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,521
- What?
- Huh?

28
00:03:05,131 --> 00:03:06,440
- What for?
- Yeah.

29
00:03:08,132 --> 00:03:09,572
I have to work on the display board,

30
00:03:11,499 --> 00:03:13,539
so you two can go to the
rehearsal room without me.

31
00:03:14,171 --> 00:03:15,172
I'm gonna head out.

32
00:03:15,856 --> 00:03:16,857
What?

33
00:03:17,099 --> 00:03:18,120
Tokyo?

34
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:19,701
What's wrong with her?

35
00:03:53,678 --> 00:03:54,800
Where are Zai and Pupay?

36
00:03:55,582 --> 00:03:58,160
You three are practically inseparable.

37
00:03:59,968 --> 00:04:00,969
Why'd you ask?

38
00:04:03,547 --> 00:04:04,720
Are you jealous?

39
00:04:05,043 --> 00:04:08,560
Oh, please. Who would be that stupid?

40
00:04:10,008 --> 00:04:12,640
Zai and Pupay are pretty
much the only friends I have.

41
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,591
When we were kids,

42
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:18,000
other parents wouldn't let their kids play
with kids like me.

43
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,361
You know why?

44
00:04:20,987 --> 00:04:22,960
Because if they ever hurt me,

45
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:25,320
my dad would...

46
00:04:29,414 --> 00:04:30,600
You just left like that.

47
00:04:31,315 --> 00:04:32,560
Didn't they get suspicious?

48
00:04:34,755 --> 00:04:35,756
Well…

49
00:04:36,419 --> 00:04:38,000
Yeah, they were suspicious.

50
00:04:38,691 --> 00:04:39,692
But...

51
00:04:40,622 --> 00:04:42,300
I just kept rambling to cover it up.

52
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,075
Here, a privacy screen protector.

53
00:04:54,136 --> 00:04:57,336
Now we're good. No one can see
what we're talking about anymore.

54
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:09,175
If it's stressing you out this much,

55
00:05:09,875 --> 00:05:11,410
why not just tell everyone?

56
00:05:15,568 --> 00:05:16,569
I can't.

57
00:05:18,054 --> 00:05:21,150
I can't tell them. I know
what things are like at home.

58
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:26,100
If I tell them, it'll
probably cause problems.

59
00:05:27,112 --> 00:05:30,320
I don't know what to do either.

60
00:05:34,574 --> 00:05:37,360
I'm OK with anything, I'll go
along with whatever you decide.

61
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:45,080
Attention, please. Ms. Phakjira
Monchaitrakul from Class 6/3,

62
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,440
please report to the
administration office immediately.

63
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:03,800
"Juliet &amp; Juliet"
(Episode 3)

64
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,560
Phakjira, have a seat.

65
00:07:18,152 --> 00:07:19,840
Phakjira and Piyathida,

66
00:07:20,136 --> 00:07:23,600
both of you can pack up all your belongings
by this afternoon and move out.

67
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:29,591
Why have you

68
00:07:30,145 --> 00:07:32,433
suddenly asked us to leave the dorm?

69
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,280
[Request to Leave the
Chantrawattana School Dormitory]

70
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,800
Did we do something wrong?

71
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:47,100
I'm the one who asked them to move you
and Pakkard out of the dorm.

72
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,200
So we can live together.

73
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:57,120
I have to work at the port here,

74
00:07:57,784 --> 00:07:58,785
so I have…

75
00:07:59,179 --> 00:08:01,475
- already bought us a new house...
- Without asking me?

76
00:08:04,432 --> 00:08:06,432
I want to stay in the
school dorm with my friends.

77
00:08:06,592 --> 00:08:07,850
I don't want to live at home.

78
00:08:14,528 --> 00:08:15,529
Miss Vee,

79
00:08:16,886 --> 00:08:18,600
I really like the dorm here.

80
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,001
I'd rather stay here, please.

81
00:08:39,368 --> 00:08:39,921
Blue.

82
00:08:43,184 --> 00:08:44,520
Can't we just talk nicely?

83
00:08:45,027 --> 00:08:46,320
It's always the same.

84
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,720
You never ask me
if I'm okay with what you decide.

85
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:53,881
How could living in a dorm
be better than living at home?

86
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:57,040
I didn't raise you
to live a difficult life.

87
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,681
I'm not struggling here.

88
00:08:59,259 --> 00:09:01,760
If anything, living at home
might be harder for me.

89
00:09:05,078 --> 00:09:06,079
Blue,

90
00:09:06,662 --> 00:09:09,040
your mom and I have
supported you all this time.

91
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:11,224
You wanted to transfer here
because of the special admission program,

92
00:09:11,248 --> 00:09:13,500
so I even moved here with you.
What more do you want?

93
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,560
You didn't let me come
here that easily for no reason.

94
00:09:19,531 --> 00:09:21,731
You were planning to move
your business here all along.

95
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,421
If you want me to believe you,

96
00:09:26,150 --> 00:09:27,600
then be honest.

97
00:09:28,512 --> 00:09:30,160
What are you really after with the Kongpurim?

98
00:09:37,998 --> 00:09:39,960
All you need to know is that

99
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,136
everything I've done has
been for our family. That's all.

100
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,240
Then just keep focusing one your business,

101
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,021
leave me out of this.

102
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:48,840
And leave my friends out of this.

103
00:10:23,446 --> 00:10:26,080
Did you pressure her into anything?

104
00:10:27,032 --> 00:10:30,120
She may be stubborn,
but she's never acted like this before.

105
00:10:32,168 --> 00:10:33,320
I didn't say anything.

106
00:10:37,392 --> 00:10:39,392
Whatever you're planning
to do, please do it soon.

107
00:10:40,048 --> 00:10:42,768
I'm worried something bad might
happen again, like it did last time.

108
00:10:59,976 --> 00:11:03,400
That's exactly why I came back here,
to settle this once and for all.

109
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,040
I won't let something
like that happen again.

110
00:11:10,064 --> 00:11:11,360
But I'm worried about her.

111
00:11:14,118 --> 00:11:15,320
Just wait and see.

112
00:11:16,518 --> 00:11:17,700
Once she runs out of money,

113
00:11:17,919 --> 00:11:19,599
she'll come crawling back home on her own.

114
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,720
Maybe then she'll finally realize

115
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,840
how important family is.

116
00:11:26,523 --> 00:11:29,160
What kind of child thinks she
can win against her parents?

117
00:11:38,976 --> 00:11:42,160
- You can use my money for now, if you need it.
- [Another cartoon commission.]

118
00:11:44,102 --> 00:11:45,103
I don't think so.

119
00:11:46,635 --> 00:11:49,120
Why not? I don't mind.

120
00:11:49,896 --> 00:11:52,200
I barely spend any money anyway.

121
00:11:54,931 --> 00:11:56,600
I don't want you to think

122
00:11:56,632 --> 00:11:59,352
I'm staying with you because of your money,
like your other friends.

123
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,360
I don't think that about you.

124
00:12:04,771 --> 00:12:07,520
I'll save it as a last resort.

125
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:20,570
When I was a kid,

126
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:24,960
my dad gave me everything I wanted.

127
00:12:25,323 --> 00:12:26,640
If I wanted something, I got it.

128
00:12:27,267 --> 00:12:30,115
But the problem was,
I didn't know how to manage it.

129
00:12:32,416 --> 00:12:34,480
You were like a princess, huh?

130
00:12:35,995 --> 00:12:37,800
Your family gave you
everything you wanted.

131
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,200
Except one thing.

132
00:12:44,691 --> 00:12:45,692
What is it?

133
00:12:47,286 --> 00:12:48,840
You can't leave your palace.

134
00:12:57,688 --> 00:12:59,850
If our families ever found out about us,

135
00:13:01,662 --> 00:13:03,560
it'd be a full-on civil war.

136
00:13:08,603 --> 00:13:10,930
We can keep it between us.

137
00:13:17,035 --> 00:13:20,280
Or we could just get out of here.

138
00:13:23,432 --> 00:13:24,800
I'm going anyway.

139
00:13:25,683 --> 00:13:27,650
My dream is

140
00:13:27,998 --> 00:13:30,600
to get into a university in Bangkok
through the quota system

141
00:13:31,176 --> 00:13:34,680
and draw or do something related to art.

142
00:13:38,059 --> 00:13:39,060
That's cool.

143
00:13:39,862 --> 00:13:41,560
I've never thought about any of that.

144
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:44,041
Why's that?

145
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,800
I mean... what do you want
to do when you grow up?

146
00:13:53,358 --> 00:13:54,359
It never crossed my mind.

147
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:01,480
Honestly, growing up,

148
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:05,241
I just did whatever Dad and Yi told me to.

149
00:14:06,910 --> 00:14:08,200
They picked my school,

150
00:14:09,427 --> 00:14:10,960
sent me to boxing lessons,

151
00:14:11,774 --> 00:14:14,600
and sometimes I'd go to
events as Dad's daughter.

152
00:14:17,740 --> 00:14:18,741
You know,

153
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:22,240
I never even had to think about
where I'd go to university.

154
00:14:24,821 --> 00:14:26,750
Dad was going to make me

155
00:14:27,576 --> 00:14:29,880
study here in the province anyway.

156
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,001
But...

157
00:14:38,104 --> 00:14:39,205
then I met you,

158
00:14:45,054 --> 00:14:47,720
and I realized that

159
00:14:48,486 --> 00:14:50,287
dreams don't have to stay in one place.

160
00:14:53,424 --> 00:14:54,960
Am I being a bad influence on you?

161
00:14:55,328 --> 00:14:57,000
Of course not.

162
00:14:59,683 --> 00:15:01,768
I just want to live my own life

163
00:15:02,486 --> 00:15:04,560
without having to do
what Dad and Yi tell me.

164
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,401
That alone would make me happy.

165
00:15:10,766 --> 00:15:14,767
Maybe leaving together

166
00:15:15,367 --> 00:15:16,960
could be the answer for both of us.

167
00:15:20,867 --> 00:15:22,520
Are you sure about going away with me?

168
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,401
Yes, I'm sure.

169
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,301
Listen.

170
00:15:32,201 --> 00:15:34,347
Moving away from home and family

171
00:15:34,758 --> 00:15:36,440
is a huge decision.

172
00:15:39,359 --> 00:15:42,880
I don't want you to come with me

173
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,760
only to regret it later.

174
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,651
Please give it some serious thought.

175
00:16:18,070 --> 00:16:20,430
I'm thinking of applying for
a scholarship to study abroad.

176
00:16:21,371 --> 00:16:22,372
What?

177
00:16:22,582 --> 00:16:23,883
Where do you want to go?

178
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:26,051
You can't even look after
yourself with us around.

179
00:16:26,744 --> 00:16:29,620
Yeah, you already sneak
out past the guards here.

180
00:16:30,638 --> 00:16:33,296
If you actually study abroad,
who's to say you won't disappear on us?

181
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:35,360
I'll make her carry a
GPS tracker at all times.

182
00:16:35,621 --> 00:16:36,622
Sounds good, Dad?

183
00:16:40,053 --> 00:16:41,360
Have you decided

184
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,880
which country you want to study in yet?

185
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,701
England.

186
00:16:49,115 --> 00:16:50,920
England? Really?

187
00:16:51,446 --> 00:16:52,766
Since when are you into football?

188
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:56,640
No, I enjoy reading Shakespeare's works.

189
00:16:58,166 --> 00:16:59,760
He was born in England,

190
00:17:00,502 --> 00:17:04,003
so I want to see his
house there for myself.

191
00:17:04,598 --> 00:17:07,720
If that's all, couldn't you
just go there on holiday?

192
00:17:11,574 --> 00:17:14,160
But my school offers a scholarship, Dad.

193
00:17:14,523 --> 00:17:16,163
We wouldn't have to pay for it ourselves.

194
00:17:18,224 --> 00:17:20,640
Well, then…

195
00:17:21,125 --> 00:17:22,400
I'll buy you a house there

196
00:17:22,926 --> 00:17:24,446
and send some people to stay with you.

197
00:17:24,683 --> 00:17:27,043
They'll take care of everything you need,
around the clock.

198
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:28,501
How about that?

199
00:17:33,291 --> 00:17:34,692
I was just saying, Dad.

200
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:40,160
With my grades, I'd be lucky to even
get into a university in Bangkok.

201
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:42,561
Study in Bangkok?

202
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:44,351
Sure, go ahead.

203
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:46,240
If it's Bangkok,

204
00:17:46,781 --> 00:17:48,782
I'll buy some land and build you a house.

205
00:17:49,288 --> 00:17:50,648
Once you graduate, we can sell it.

206
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,900
That's not a bad idea.
It'd be a property investment too.

207
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,520
It was just a thought, Dad.

208
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:05,360
I'm not even sure my scores would get me
into a university in Bangkok.

209
00:18:05,837 --> 00:18:07,480
They require pretty high scores.

210
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,161
I was only asking.

211
00:18:30,406 --> 00:18:33,640
She's not picking up.
Maybe her dad won't let her out.

212
00:18:37,054 --> 00:18:39,160
What's with all the spending lately?

213
00:18:39,896 --> 00:18:40,897
You win the lottery?

214
00:18:41,363 --> 00:18:44,000
Of course not. I'll just borrow
some money from Tokyo.

215
00:18:45,526 --> 00:18:49,080
So you're gonna call and
wake her up this early on her day off?

216
00:18:49,424 --> 00:18:50,425
That's right.

217
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:57,920
Hey, I didn't order this one.

218
00:18:58,131 --> 00:18:59,132
I ordered it for you two.

219
00:19:01,464 --> 00:19:02,465
Go on.

220
00:19:03,790 --> 00:19:04,791
Enjoy it.

221
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:08,358
Umm…Yi.

222
00:19:08,966 --> 00:19:11,720
If it's about this round's lottery payment,

223
00:19:11,814 --> 00:19:14,815
Mom was wondering if she
could have until next week.

224
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:18,520
- She didn't win anything this time.
- Hey, I'm not here about that.

225
00:19:20,446 --> 00:19:21,760
I've got some work for you.

226
00:19:23,891 --> 00:19:25,200
Get it done,

227
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,880
and I'll reduce what your parents owe.

228
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:33,400
What kind of job?

229
00:19:34,621 --> 00:19:37,440
It's easy.

230
00:19:39,722 --> 00:19:41,193
You girls can handle it.

231
00:19:42,126 --> 00:19:45,160
Just find out who
Tokyo's new best friend is.

232
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:48,480
A friend? Who?

233
00:19:48,947 --> 00:19:50,840
That Monchaitrakul girl.

234
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,680
Someone spotted her with Tokyo
at the market, just the two of them.

235
00:19:56,264 --> 00:19:58,800
Find out what they talk
about, what they're up to,

236
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:01,680
and how close they
are. I want every detail.

237
00:20:02,985 --> 00:20:04,580
But from what I've seen at school,

238
00:20:04,591 --> 00:20:07,160
they don't seem that close.

239
00:20:07,592 --> 00:20:11,134
I don't think you'll get much out of this.

240
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:20,601
Then just let me know
if you make any progress

241
00:20:20,641 --> 00:20:22,960
or find out anything else.

242
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,501
Okay?

243
00:20:32,128 --> 00:20:35,680
But if I find out you knew
something and didn't tell me,

244
00:20:37,748 --> 00:20:39,449
I'll show up at your doorstep.

245
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:44,401
Got it.

246
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:19,221
Hey.

247
00:21:21,123 --> 00:21:23,960
Isn't that the character Blue
drew for the library board?

248
00:21:24,739 --> 00:21:25,740
Yeah, I know.

249
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,720
[Tokyo: I've figured it
out. I'll take a gap year.]

250
00:21:29,740 --> 00:21:31,076
[It'll give me an excuse
to find myself. Good idea?]

251
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:32,620
[Blue: That's your idea? Think again.]

252
00:21:32,700 --> 00:21:34,677
[Tokyo: Hey, I don't have
a clear goal like you do.]

253
00:21:34,701 --> 00:21:36,936
[Blue: Take your time.
You'll figure it out. I'll help.]

254
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:37,976
[Blue: Think about what you like doing.]

255
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,001
[Tokyo: Sleeping.]

256
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,680
[Blue: What else do you like?]

257
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,160
[Tokyo: You.]

258
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,476
[Blue: Is this really the
time to joke around?]

259
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,577
[Tokyo: Reading novels and comics.]

260
00:21:45,601 --> 00:21:47,002
[Blue: Almost at the library.]

261
00:21:47,102 --> 00:21:48,103
[Tokyo: Me too.]

262
00:22:16,464 --> 00:22:17,465
What?

263
00:22:19,611 --> 00:22:21,331
Didn't you finish with the library's board?

264
00:22:24,203 --> 00:22:26,600
- That's right.
- What are you doing here?

265
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:30,561
I am…

266
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:37,301
I…

267
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:42,360
I'd like to join the literature club.

268
00:22:43,856 --> 00:22:44,857
Really?

269
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,321
That's right.

270
00:22:48,566 --> 00:22:49,720
But that's a good thing.

271
00:22:50,064 --> 00:22:53,400
Maybe Mr. Po would be willing to
fund some new books for the library.

272
00:22:55,547 --> 00:22:56,548
You two,

273
00:22:59,486 --> 00:23:01,155
sort these books

274
00:23:01,187 --> 00:23:03,980
by category and put
them on the proper shelves.

275
00:23:11,059 --> 00:23:12,060
As for you,

276
00:23:12,808 --> 00:23:16,360
sort these books by category
and put them on the right shelves.

277
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:17,800
Don't mix them up.

278
00:23:20,638 --> 00:23:21,880
All of them?

279
00:23:22,390 --> 00:23:23,391
That's right.

280
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:32,501
Wait.

281
00:23:33,501 --> 00:23:36,180
Ask Mr. Po to donate
some new books too, okay?

282
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,201
Sure.

283
00:23:40,235 --> 00:23:41,860
Don't drop any of them.

284
00:24:02,171 --> 00:24:03,560
♪ To you ♪

285
00:24:05,542 --> 00:24:07,600
♪ The one who means everything to me ♪

286
00:24:09,651 --> 00:24:13,480
♪ I'll be waiting to walk beside you ♪

287
00:24:15,171 --> 00:24:17,760
♪ Our dreams won't be far away ♪

288
00:24:18,736 --> 00:24:20,000
♪ But you ♪

289
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:25,860
♪ slowly faded away and changed ♪

290
00:24:26,221 --> 00:24:30,000
♪ My journey toward my
dreams came to an end ♪

291
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:34,560
♪ No matter how long it takes ♪

292
00:24:35,352 --> 00:24:36,753
♪ I keep waiting ♪

293
00:24:39,744 --> 00:24:41,045
♪ I'll be waiting ♪

294
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,560
♪ Though it may be only a dream ♪

295
00:24:45,168 --> 00:24:49,000
♪ Of a better day ♪

296
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:52,800
♪ When you return to me ♪

297
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:57,040
♪ There'll be love and everything we need ♪

298
00:24:57,150 --> 00:25:01,040
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

299
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:05,200
♪ There'll be the two of
us, walking side by side ♪

300
00:25:08,254 --> 00:25:09,500
♪ To you ♪

301
00:25:09,855 --> 00:25:13,300
♪ Who give love depth ♪

302
00:25:13,822 --> 00:25:17,823
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

303
00:25:18,123 --> 00:25:21,840
♪ There'll be love and everything we need ♪

304
00:25:24,944 --> 00:25:26,280
♪ To you ♪

305
00:25:26,320 --> 00:25:29,880
♪ Who give love depth ♪

306
00:25:30,235 --> 00:25:34,080
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

307
00:25:34,496 --> 00:25:38,400
♪ There'll be the two of
us, walking side by side ♪

308
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:42,241
♪ To you ♪

309
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:46,280
♪ Who give love depth ♪

310
00:25:46,616 --> 00:25:50,720
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

311
00:25:51,083 --> 00:25:53,584
♪ You're the one who made my love... ♪

312
00:25:55,355 --> 00:25:57,500
♪ become real ♪

313
00:26:00,286 --> 00:26:01,287
Hey!

314
00:26:03,043 --> 00:26:05,480
There you are. I've been
looking everywhere for you.

315
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:07,361
I'm sorry. I'm so so sorry.

316
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:11,801
So, are you serious
about studying in England?

317
00:26:13,339 --> 00:26:14,768
I…

318
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:19,080
Our school doesn't offer a scholarship
to study in England

319
00:26:19,100 --> 00:26:20,660
like you told your family.

320
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:25,640
I don't really want to go, actually.

321
00:26:26,141 --> 00:26:28,560
It's just that some of my friends

322
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:30,102
who do well in school were going there,

323
00:26:30,126 --> 00:26:31,480
so I wanted to go too.

324
00:26:32,127 --> 00:26:34,128
You wanted to follow
your friends there to study?

325
00:26:34,211 --> 00:26:35,907
Oh, dear.

326
00:26:36,120 --> 00:26:37,121
There's no need to go.

327
00:26:37,150 --> 00:26:40,151
Why envy people who
get better grades than you?

328
00:26:40,627 --> 00:26:42,840
Your family has so much
more for others to envy.

329
00:26:42,974 --> 00:26:45,334
You've clearly got a better
start in life than most people.

330
00:26:45,454 --> 00:26:47,406
What's the point of studying in England?

331
00:26:47,464 --> 00:26:48,480
Those students will just come back

332
00:26:48,504 --> 00:26:52,640
and work for wealthy business owners
like your family anyway.

333
00:26:53,966 --> 00:26:55,500
I think

334
00:26:55,923 --> 00:26:59,760
you'd be better off thinking about
how to take over the family business.

335
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:04,622
So, what's made you take your studies
so seriously lately?

336
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:07,760
Could it be...

337
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:10,440
that new girl pressuring you?

338
00:27:11,763 --> 00:27:13,964
Oh, she's not pressuring me.

339
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:15,641
It's nothing.

340
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,881
- Thanks for asking.
- Sure.

341
00:27:27,700 --> 00:27:28,721
You're not leaving?

342
00:27:29,907 --> 00:27:31,000
I need to find a book.

343
00:27:31,408 --> 00:27:32,409
I see.

344
00:27:54,438 --> 00:27:55,439
Dad.

345
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:58,605
All our distributors have pulled out of
their transportation deals with us.

346
00:27:58,629 --> 00:28:00,029
They're undercutting us like crazy.

347
00:28:03,691 --> 00:28:05,040
First the port,

348
00:28:05,963 --> 00:28:07,763
now they're sticking
their noses in here too?

349
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:10,600
They started in the neighboring district.

350
00:28:10,795 --> 00:28:13,250
Now they're moving
further into our territory.

351
00:28:13,918 --> 00:28:15,240
If this keeps up,

352
00:28:15,592 --> 00:28:17,400
our other businesses could be in trouble.

353
00:28:17,827 --> 00:28:19,747
You can't let them
disrespect us like this, Dad.

354
00:28:26,067 --> 00:28:27,068
Then...

355
00:28:28,419 --> 00:28:30,420
how about paying his daughter a visit?

356
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:33,601
What?

357
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:37,721
If you're going to take over from me,

358
00:28:38,610 --> 00:28:41,160
you need to prove you're worthy.

359
00:28:52,368 --> 00:28:53,369
Okay.

360
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:08,140
- Hello.
- This way, please.

361
00:29:17,740 --> 00:29:18,741
Okay.

362
00:29:19,640 --> 00:29:20,641
This seat?

363
00:29:26,491 --> 00:29:27,492
What?

364
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,920
You came to eat without inviting us?

365
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:36,120
What brings you here?

366
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:38,480
We followed you here, obviously.

367
00:29:38,830 --> 00:29:40,990
What's so weird about that?
We come here all the time.

368
00:29:54,072 --> 00:29:56,050
Ooh, fish tofu with cheese!

369
00:30:10,560 --> 00:30:11,761
You don't want it?

370
00:30:13,014 --> 00:30:15,494
Nope, I want something else.

371
00:30:40,350 --> 00:30:41,351
You want some?

372
00:30:42,664 --> 00:30:43,690
Thanks.

373
00:30:55,736 --> 00:30:57,470
- Zai.
- What?

374
00:30:58,488 --> 00:31:00,368
Since when do you like
cheese-filled fish tofu?

375
00:31:00,880 --> 00:31:02,560
I've always liked it, okay?

376
00:31:04,441 --> 00:31:05,960
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

377
00:31:09,424 --> 00:31:12,440
Hey, if you're not gonna eat it,
why are you taking it from me?

378
00:31:12,510 --> 00:31:15,160
I wasn't taking it from
you. I was gonna feed you.

379
00:31:15,283 --> 00:31:17,123
- Hey, it's still hot.
- Eat it while it's hot.

380
00:31:22,608 --> 00:31:23,609
Is it good?

381
00:31:25,720 --> 00:31:26,920
Damn! It's too hot.

382
00:31:46,254 --> 00:31:47,255
What are you doing?

383
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:49,780
I'm just stiff. I was stretching.

384
00:32:12,248 --> 00:32:14,281
Hey, I'll be right back.

385
00:32:15,086 --> 00:32:17,526
- Where are you going?
- I'm going to get some Tokyo pancakes.

386
00:32:17,944 --> 00:32:18,945
I'll be right back.

387
00:32:30,131 --> 00:32:32,360
Two custard-filled pancakes, please.

388
00:32:58,600 --> 00:33:01,200
[Tokyo: Sorry. I'll find a way
to send those two home ASAP.]

389
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,760
[Blue: It's okay. We can
go on a date another day.]

390
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:12,560
[Tokyo: Okay. I'll bring you
some custard-filled pancakes.]

391
00:33:33,980 --> 00:33:37,160
A Monchaitrakul shouldn't
be out here like this.

392
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:45,360
Don't you know it's dangerous?

393
00:33:47,995 --> 00:33:49,160
Dangerous how?

394
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:50,721
Come on.

395
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:53,480
Because everyone in this
town is with the Kongpurims.

396
00:33:58,920 --> 00:33:59,921
Then

397
00:34:00,400 --> 00:34:02,240
how come people are
still working at the port

398
00:34:02,595 --> 00:34:03,800
like nothing's changed?

399
00:34:05,235 --> 00:34:07,680
- You dare talk back to the boss? Huh?
- Hey!

400
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:10,280
Can you really hurt a girl?

401
00:34:18,112 --> 00:34:20,100
We usually leave girls alone.

402
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:23,000
But when it comes to the Monchaitrakuls,

403
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:25,080
no one's getting spared.

404
00:34:25,820 --> 00:34:27,100
Not even women or children.

405
00:34:34,770 --> 00:34:35,771
Hey.

406
00:34:36,595 --> 00:34:37,596
Hi.

407
00:34:38,680 --> 00:34:39,800
You're eating here too?

408
00:34:43,083 --> 00:34:45,040
No. I'm here to collect the interest.

409
00:34:46,104 --> 00:34:48,105
Who are you here with?

410
00:35:03,428 --> 00:35:04,760
With Zai and Pupay, of course.

411
00:35:07,900 --> 00:35:08,901
Yeah?

412
00:35:15,891 --> 00:35:16,892
Yeah.

413
00:35:38,486 --> 00:35:39,520
What did you do?

414
00:35:42,917 --> 00:35:44,360
I burned my hand on an iron.

415
00:35:47,060 --> 00:35:48,061
I told you,

416
00:35:48,245 --> 00:35:50,685
getting mixed up with the
Kongpurims is nothing but trouble..

417
00:35:51,990 --> 00:35:53,320
If that burn doesn't heal,

418
00:35:53,968 --> 00:35:55,280
you'd better see a doctor soon.

419
00:35:55,984 --> 00:35:57,800
We're visiting my dad's grave soon.

420
00:35:58,096 --> 00:36:00,376
If your dad sees your hand like that,
he'll get mad again.

421
00:36:01,408 --> 00:36:02,409
Oh, right.

422
00:36:03,382 --> 00:36:05,120
Your dad's death anniversary is coming up.

423
00:36:08,383 --> 00:36:11,800
Next time, come up with a better lie.

424
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:15,725
That's not a burn from
an iron. I'm not that stupid.

425
00:36:17,816 --> 00:36:19,960
Besides, now that you've moved here,

426
00:36:20,557 --> 00:36:23,500
I'm all you've got so let me help you.

427
00:36:26,125 --> 00:36:27,880
You don't have to keep things from me.

428
00:36:33,456 --> 00:36:36,240
Are you free tomorrow?

429
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:04,601
What is going on?

430
00:37:05,878 --> 00:37:07,158
You brought me here for a fight?

431
00:37:08,731 --> 00:37:11,280
- Should've brought more backup.
- Nope.

432
00:37:22,774 --> 00:37:23,840
(In unison) We're dating.

433
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:29,520
I'd rather you called me here for a fight.

434
00:37:34,907 --> 00:37:35,960
I need to ask you this:

435
00:37:36,691 --> 00:37:39,456
do you really think two people
from rival mafia families in this province

436
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:40,960
could ever make a relationship work?

437
00:37:41,720 --> 00:37:42,960
You think it's gonna last?

438
00:37:44,640 --> 00:37:46,739
We're trying.

439
00:37:49,315 --> 00:37:50,860
As for whether we'll last,

440
00:37:51,683 --> 00:37:53,520
can we at least give it a shot?

441
00:37:58,680 --> 00:37:59,681
Sure.

442
00:38:01,847 --> 00:38:04,760
You've already made up your minds.
What are you asking me for?

443
00:38:08,395 --> 00:38:09,860
Then you two have to promise me

444
00:38:10,496 --> 00:38:13,480
you'll tell me if anything happens.

445
00:38:18,203 --> 00:38:19,204
I'm worried about you.

446
00:38:21,654 --> 00:38:22,655
I promise.

447
00:38:23,622 --> 00:38:25,222
I'll tell you first if anything happens,

448
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:27,161
okay?

449
00:38:30,915 --> 00:38:31,916
You promise?

450
00:38:33,040 --> 00:38:34,680
I promise.

451
00:38:39,512 --> 00:38:40,513
So this is why

452
00:38:41,646 --> 00:38:44,326
you don't want to move out of the dorm
and live with your dad, huh?

453
00:38:46,300 --> 00:38:47,301
Yeah.

454
00:38:55,109 --> 00:38:56,110
Hey.

455
00:38:58,680 --> 00:39:00,040
[Pakkard, please don't be mad.]

456
00:39:05,936 --> 00:39:06,937
Just take it.

457
00:39:12,896 --> 00:39:14,400
"Pakkard, please don't be mad."

458
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:58,200
My mouth's messy too.
How about wiping mine?

459
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:12,656
[Tokyo: Don't forget to put ointment
on your wound so it'll heal faster.]

460
00:40:12,680 --> 00:40:14,681
[Blue: Pakkard already
helped me with that.]

461
00:40:14,690 --> 00:40:16,168
If the Monchaitrakuls keep this up,

462
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:22,360
we'll have to handle it
the same way we did 17 years ago.

463
00:40:27,387 --> 00:40:28,388
It's okay.

464
00:40:29,179 --> 00:40:30,200
I will handle this.

465
00:40:31,483 --> 00:40:34,160
All you need to do is clean up afterward.

466
00:40:39,624 --> 00:40:40,625
Got it.

467
00:40:56,700 --> 00:40:58,320
You can't even take care of yourself

468
00:40:59,363 --> 00:41:00,760
and we're worried about you.

469
00:41:01,315 --> 00:41:03,100
How can we let you out of our sight?

470
00:41:04,380 --> 00:41:05,381
Sure I can.

471
00:41:05,739 --> 00:41:07,100
I'm not a little girl anymore.

472
00:41:08,700 --> 00:41:12,360
If you're still acting on impulse
and can't even support yourself,

473
00:41:13,211 --> 00:41:14,651
you're not grown up yet, sweetheart.

474
00:41:20,371 --> 00:41:21,400
Tell me honestly.

475
00:41:23,821 --> 00:41:25,880
Why don't you want to
move back home with me?

476
00:41:39,507 --> 00:41:40,520
Are you seeing someone?

477
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:49,500
I don't mind if you are.

478
00:41:50,691 --> 00:41:52,840
You can date with us around, sweetheart.

479
00:41:53,566 --> 00:41:56,900
Whether it's a girl or a boy,
it's perfectly normal. I understand that.

480
00:41:57,347 --> 00:41:59,248
It's not about that, Mom.

481
00:42:01,363 --> 00:42:02,800
I can handle it myself.

482
00:42:14,315 --> 00:42:15,920
Or is the reason you can't tell me

483
00:42:18,832 --> 00:42:20,120
that they're a Kongpurim?

484
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:46,160
[The accident 17 years ago]

485
00:42:56,619 --> 00:42:57,620
Mom.

486
00:42:58,504 --> 00:43:00,100
Mom, please don't tell Dad.

487
00:43:00,960 --> 00:43:02,920
I don't want things to
get any more complicated.

488
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:05,041
Blue,

489
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:10,600
your dad isn't being unreasonable
or just holding some senseless grudge.

490
00:43:12,899 --> 00:43:14,400
Someone actually died

491
00:43:15,080 --> 00:43:17,481
because of the feud
between our two families,

492
00:43:19,081 --> 00:43:21,960
Uncle Wirat, Pakkarn's father.

493
00:43:23,240 --> 00:43:26,541
[A Businessman, Wirat,
brutally murdered in a luxury car]

494
00:43:30,144 --> 00:43:32,840
We have proof,

495
00:43:34,784 --> 00:43:37,240
but they've got powerful
people behind them.

496
00:43:38,283 --> 00:43:40,120
That's why we can't get justice.

497
00:43:44,475 --> 00:43:45,600
You understand

498
00:43:47,152 --> 00:43:49,900
this is more than just kids'
stuff now, don't you, sweetheart?

499
00:44:01,523 --> 00:44:03,000
I'll talk to your dad

500
00:44:03,840 --> 00:44:06,160
about letting you stay at the dorm.

501
00:44:09,336 --> 00:44:10,337
Blue,

502
00:44:12,627 --> 00:44:14,840
you have to cut ties with that family.

503
00:44:17,294 --> 00:44:18,295
For your own good.

504
00:44:25,917 --> 00:44:26,918
I should go.

505
00:44:35,363 --> 00:44:37,120
Maybe leaving together

506
00:44:38,611 --> 00:44:40,160
could be the answer for both of us.

507
00:44:43,491 --> 00:44:45,100
Are you sure about going away with me?

508
00:44:47,016 --> 00:44:48,017
Yes, I'm sure.

509
00:45:33,360 --> 00:45:36,200
[Can you come meet me
at Auntie's stall by the pier?]

510
00:45:43,069 --> 00:45:44,070
Do you think

511
00:45:45,251 --> 00:45:47,130
what my mom said is true?

512
00:45:49,753 --> 00:45:53,063
I don't know. True or
made up, who gives a shit?

513
00:45:54,702 --> 00:45:55,703
Why's that?

514
00:45:57,331 --> 00:45:58,332
Be honest.

515
00:45:59,059 --> 00:46:01,699
You don't have to spare my feelings
just because I'm dating Tokyo.

516
00:46:03,155 --> 00:46:04,850
I'm not trying to comfort you.

517
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:08,141
There's no clear proof
the Kongpurims did it.

518
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:11,280
Both sides tell the story to
make themselves look good.

519
00:46:14,649 --> 00:46:17,800
What is your side of the story?

520
00:46:20,910 --> 00:46:22,300
The truth from my side?

521
00:46:22,911 --> 00:46:25,416
After my dad died,

522
00:46:25,875 --> 00:46:28,600
I've been living here with
relatives on my mom's side.

523
00:46:29,963 --> 00:46:31,603
The Kongpurims have paid for my education

524
00:46:31,850 --> 00:46:34,000
through scholarships
ever since I was a kid.

525
00:46:34,584 --> 00:46:37,185
And they've never treated
people in the community badly.

526
00:46:37,760 --> 00:46:40,150
Do you really expect me to
believe they're bad people?

527
00:46:45,040 --> 00:46:46,920
Honestly,

528
00:46:48,147 --> 00:46:51,120
I don't care about what
happened in the past.

529
00:46:51,976 --> 00:46:53,200
What matters to me is today.

530
00:46:54,048 --> 00:46:56,080
If they're not treating you badly now,

531
00:46:56,795 --> 00:46:58,140
then I still believe in them.

532
00:47:08,691 --> 00:47:10,240
There's something that can't wait.

533
00:47:10,712 --> 00:47:13,513
I want to talk to you about it right now.

534
00:47:16,416 --> 00:47:18,016
You already knew about this, didn't you?

535
00:47:19,040 --> 00:47:20,041
About…

536
00:47:21,435 --> 00:47:23,675
Your uncle who died 17 years ago.

537
00:47:31,952 --> 00:47:33,720
Honestly, I'm not sure

538
00:47:34,219 --> 00:47:35,920
about what happened either.

539
00:47:36,675 --> 00:47:38,460
I'm not sure if my family did it.

540
00:47:46,750 --> 00:47:47,751
But …

541
00:47:49,551 --> 00:47:50,800
I understand

542
00:47:51,502 --> 00:47:53,560
if you don't want to be with me.

543
00:47:55,518 --> 00:47:57,880
What happened was really terrible.

544
00:48:02,232 --> 00:48:05,062
Once I find proof that

545
00:48:05,563 --> 00:48:07,627
the Kongpurims weren't responsible,

546
00:48:09,302 --> 00:48:12,240
- we can get back together then.
- I don't care about any of that.

547
00:48:15,547 --> 00:48:18,860
Why should we have to
inherit a feud the adults started?

548
00:48:24,915 --> 00:48:25,916
Besides,

549
00:48:28,397 --> 00:48:29,840
I like you.

550
00:48:32,291 --> 00:48:34,000
I have no reason to stop seeing you.

551
00:48:43,368 --> 00:48:44,800
You really believe that?

552
00:48:45,710 --> 00:48:46,711
Yeah.

553
00:48:49,560 --> 00:48:51,280
They made this mess.

554
00:48:52,718 --> 00:48:54,130
Let them deal with it.

555
00:50:08,710 --> 00:50:10,270
(Next Episode)
This is Tong.

556
00:50:10,500 --> 00:50:13,480
Representing Sappakan Sueksa.
Why don't you get to know each other?

557
00:50:14,001 --> 00:50:15,676
Tong invited me to
take art classes with him.

558
00:50:15,700 --> 00:50:17,200
Your ex?

559
00:50:19,288 --> 00:50:22,889
Tokyo, you're not dating that
family's daughter, are you?

560
00:50:24,046 --> 00:50:26,200
I won't let it go for sure.

561
00:50:26,675 --> 00:50:28,304
You're putting Blue
in a difficult position.

562
00:50:28,328 --> 00:50:29,848
If you truly want what's best for her,

563
00:50:30,280 --> 00:50:31,281
let her go.
